# CMZ, the issuer's own proof that it issued with the key it
# published.  P fixes the MAC point it chose, PK0 its public key, and
# R ties the two together.  The bilinear fact behind R is linearised
# by publishing P first and writing R against it, so no equation
# multiplies two secrets -- which is what keeps the statement inside
# the Maurer class at all.  Examples/Cmz.v, issuer_stmt.
secrets b x0
claims  b x0
eq  P     A  1
eq  PK0   1  B
eq  R     K  P

# An instance: one distinct generator per base name, so the
# environment is faithful and the verdict above transfers to it.
# The exponents are ours and carry no meaning; every element of a
# prime-order group is a generator power, so this is simply a way
# to write distinct elements down.
point A  2
point B  3
point K  5
point P  7
